Z||000007||BBBAD GT||07-22-2001||11:16 PM||||Please don't lable all 5.0's as being slow, just as your Fiero is modified, there are about 10 times more 5.0's that are heavily modified.  Here is a video of my 5.0, running 11.13 @ 127 mph in the quarter mile, then driven home 100 miles.  <BR> <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/Quartermile.asf" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/Quartermile.asf</A> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">         <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale *SOLD*</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rogue_Ant||07-22-2001||11:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Whats in your car?  Cause of all the mustangs the 5.0 is a beast. If yours is stock she wasnt racing you....Now then if it was a newer mustang with the 4.6 then thats a different story...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, I used to own an 95 GT (last year they made the 5.0 but with the new body style)<BR>They are alright, but I would get ate-up by the T/A and Camero guys all the time.  I would take a 96-98 4.6 as those were not as powerful as the 5.0s, but since 99 they redesigned the heads and put out a lot more power, they would beat me.<P>Rogue<BR>||||reg||4
