Z||000015||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||07-23-2001||04:48 AM||||Mustang GTs were not very fast until they got fuel injection in about 86 or 87.  <P>A buddy had an 83 GT with the 5.0 and it was really slow.  I mean surprisingly slow.  <P>A Fiero GT in 1985 would give a Mustang GT in 1985 a good run for it's money.  They were both in the low 7s 0 to 60 MPH.<P>After 1988, the Mustangs were all pretty quick.  I do believe a 3800 s/c could beat most any basic Mustang GT.  This does not include SVT Cobras (except the wimpy 98s), Saleens, and supercharged Mustang GTs.  Those cars are really fast.||||reg||6
