Z||000023||99BlackZ||07-23-2001||11:10 PM||||Apparantly most of you guys' experiences with 5.0's are with people who cannot drive.<BR>87 - 93 5.0 5sp's are mid to high 14 second cars all day long.  I had a 95 with only headers, 2.5" exhaust and 3:73 gears that did a 14.59@95mph at Beech Bend Raceway.  <BR>That was on street tires with little traction. Had to feather it off the line.<BR>That fully loaded sucker with me in it weighed 3600lbs. And that was on a 90+degree fourth of July.!!!  The older ones weighed several hundred pounds less and could do that stock.  It doesn't take much to put one in the 13's.  I later put a GT40 intake on mine and underdrive pulleys.  I'm certain that on a cool day, it would have broken into the 13.9's if not 14.0's with that setup.  I've had 2 fiero's (v-6's) and 4 5.0's and I can tell you that 5.0's are way faster and much easier to make even faster.<BR>Please don't flame me because I love fiero's as well, just for different reasons.  I think they are great cars, but they just aren't normally drag strip terrors.  (I know they can be, just aren't normally)||||reg||12
Z||000024||StuGood||07-23-2001||11:28 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BENGAL4:<BR><B>...We pull up to a stoplight and the was a girlin a 5.0 Mustang GT...She had a car's length lead on me, until I hit second gear. After that she was toast. My GT has so much low end torque, it is unreal...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>What impressed me about this account, is that there were two guys in the Fiero, and a girl in the Mustang.  Unless she was of the "hefty" persuasion, and/or you guys are awful scrawny, you beat her even with a 150-pound (roughly?) weight handicap!  <P>And I'm guessing while you're not horsing around (whenever <B>that</B> might be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )the 3800 probably gets decent fuel mileage to boot!  That's it- If I spend my tax refund on a 3800 conversion, you guys are partly to blame, now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||6
