Z||000026||BENGAL4||07-25-2001||06:14 PM||||Stu,<P>the girl was normal size, I however, am not. I weigh around 270 and Boilermaker has to be around 170 or so.<P>Black99Z,<P>As you can tell from my sig, my Fiero is not normal. No way would I have attempted to race her with a stock 2.8. That's why I spent all the $$.<P>I think in this case, my Grandmother could be driving the GT and it would still blow the 5.0 doors off. <P>Come on up to Cincinnati and I will make a believer out of you.BTW, where is Guston anyway? I happen to bleed orange and black from 1 arm, and blue and white from the other.<P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 Series II S/C||||reg||10
Z||000027||99BlackZ||07-25-2001||09:19 PM||||Bengal4, Yes, I noticed your sig.<BR>I'll be that is a sweet ride.<BR>I was mostly referring (some) of the other posts that claimed 5.0's were slow.<BR>I've noticed over the years that how fast a car is, is a matter of perspecive.  (If my ??? car is this fast, then everything slower is a dog) ;o)<BR>Guston is out in the middle of nowhere.<BR>About 40 minutes SW of Louisville, in Meade County.<BR>What does that 3.8 Supercharged GT do in the quarter?<P>I don't have a Mustang anymore. 99BlackZ is a ZX2.  Needed the MPG since I work in Louisville.<BR>(If you're wondering why I'm on this site to begin with, It's because I've owned 2 Fiero's in the past and still like them.  Just like to keep up with what's going on with them.<P>Later,<BR>Z<P>||||reg||1
