Z||000031||BBBAD GT||07-26-2001||09:55 AM||||This is getting rather childish now. <P>Bengal4's car is pretty awsome, and would likely take any stock 5.0 taking out driver error. <P>For some reason, it seems nobody here ever runs into a 5.0 that has been tweeked (when I say tweeked, I mean the basic bolt-ons that'll make them run low 13's without much effort, modified in my book is at least heads/cam/intake).  But I think I know why:<P>A guy with a modified Stang won't take the effort/risk to race a Fiero, just because (no offense) its a Fiero on the surface, and its rare for anybody to see a Fiero run 12's and wouldn't be much of a challenge.  The Stang guy has nothing to win, but everything to lose because he should wipe the Fiero's butt.  <P>Hope I didn't offend any Fiero owners (I had two myself), but I've said this before months ago in a 5.0/Fiero thread.<P><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">         <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale *SOLD*</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||13
